NanoCore in development

Binary SIESTA files
-------------------
from NanoCore import siestaio

cell, mesh, rho = siestaio.read_grid('sample.RHO')
siestaio.write_grid(cell, mesh, rho, file_path='copy.RHO')

Grid values have shape (nspin, nx, ny, nz); file units are unchanged.
read_dm(file_path) returns nb, ns, numd, listdptr, listd, dm.
write_dm(*data, file_path='copy.DM') uses the original two-integer DM
header; additional fields from newer input headers are not preserved.

read_wfsx(file_path), read_hsx(file_path), read_dim(file_path), and
read_pld(file_path, MAXA, MAXO) support the legacy little-endian layouts
of the original readers. Other format versions and NetCDF are not covered.
read_pld returns ISA once: RMAXO, IPHORB, INDXUO, DATM, ISA, LASTO,
CELL, NSC, XA. These functions are independent of the Siesta object.

Planar averages
--------------
from NanoCore import s2

coordinate, values = s2.planeaverage_grid(target='vh', axis='z', file_path='sample.VH')

Without file_path, the input is <label>.<TARGET>, with label from simobj
when provided, otherwise label='siesta'. Targets VH/VT return eV;
RHO/DRHO return e/Ang**3. Coordinates start at zero in Ang. Axes 0/1/2
(or x/y/z) select lattice planes; spin components are averaged, not summed.
Only arrays are returned; no PAV file or external macroave call is made.
planeaverage_grid replaces get_hartree_pot_z.
